// OpenZ (GPL-3.0) - Level 16, round 5e: the data of the plants at the map's edge and outside it (made off the engine from the level's
// plants as the game draws them, the level's own map and the map's own plants, every number measured first; the game checks it again
// before it uses any of it):
//  - RimKinds / RimSources: the kinds a plant outside the map may be, and per kind the map's own upright plants of its full model
//    whose TRUE crown (the widest horizontal extent of its own points) is at most RimCap (a new plant is a copy of one: its mesh, its
//    materials, its size, turned about the upright);
//  - RimTreeMix / RimSmallMix / RimWetMix: the map's own mix (the trees without the big kinds), as RimKinds indices and weights;
//  - RimNew: the rim ring's new plants on the rim floor (kind, the map plant it copies, its foot, its turn), per cell the small plants
//    first, then the trees and palms, each in a fixed rank (the game places them in this order while the cell stays inside its cost;
//    the rest stand only in the start flyover's low look);
//  - RimBudget: per cell the most its new plants may cost: far triangles (what its plants outside the map cost round 4 at the widest
//    zoom, times the largest scale with which no view the camera can reach at the wide zooms draws more than round 4), near
//    triangles and objects (round 4's near);
//  - RimEdge: the plants within RimEdgeBand m inside the map line on a cliff top or rim that are drawn simplified or wider than the
//    cap, and every simplified tree of the band wherever it stands: the full model of the map that stands in for each (the closest
//    kind under the cap), its turn; RimEdgeSeats: the parrots' seats on four of them, on the new crown.
